.TH CHTTPCLIENT_SET_CONNECT_TIMEOUT 3 "2026-10-01" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_set_connect_timeout \- set the TCP connect timeout
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_set_connect_timeout(chttpcli cli, uint64_t us);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function sets the maximum time for the phase of the TCP
connection, which for HTTPS also covers the TLS handshake. Give 0 to
turn the timeout off, which is the default. Every other value is
honoured as a limit, however far away it lies: a value too large for
the clock to reach, such as UINT64_MAX, saturates to the latest
deadline that the clock can hold, and never wraps into the past.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli   The client handle. It must not be CHTTPCLI_INVALID.
us    The timeout in microseconds. 0 means no timeout.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success      The client has the new timeout.
ccol_invalid_args cli is CHTTPCLI_INVALID, or a stale handle of a
                  client that is already destroyed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_set_request_timeout (3)
